  "label": "The man is mapped as 'a real life picasso painting'",
  "description": "The textual phrase 'a real life picasso painting' is mapped onto the visual entity 'man'. The man's strained, confused facial expression is used to visually represent the absurd and self-deprecating idea of being so aesthetically unappealing or artistically inept that one resembles a Picasso painting. This mapping is central to the meme's humor and relies on the visual material (the man's expression) to embody the textual metaphor (Picasso painting).",
